class:: Lifestoch
summary:: ALife birth-death breakpoint population
related:: Classes/Diststoch, Classes/Varperiod, Classes/Ecostoch
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic

description::

The breakpoint oscillator reimagined as a living population. Each waveform breakpoint is
an agent with an energy level; every cycle it gains energy below the carrying capacity
(code::growth:: vs code::crowding:: × population), reproduces when well-fed (splitting,
the child inheriting a mutated amplitude), and dies when starved. Birth and death replace
the random walk, so the number of breakpoints, and thus the waveform's timbral
complexity, self-grows and self-prunes around an equilibrium population.

The fundamental stays at code::freq:: regardless of population (the segment subdivision
adapts, as in link::Classes/Varperiod::), so the population dynamics are heard as breathing
timbre rather than pitch drift. code::maxCPs:: is fixed at build time.

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: freq
Fundamental frequency (Hz). Default 110.
argument:: maxCPs
Maximum population / allocated breakpoints (fixed). Default 64.
argument:: growth
Per-cycle energy gain (food). Higher = larger carrying capacity. Default 0.2.
argument:: crowding
Per-capita energy cost of crowding. Carrying capacity ≈ growth/crowding. Default 0.01.
argument:: birthThresh
Energy needed to reproduce. Default 1.0.
argument:: mutate
Amplitude mutation range for offspring. Default 0.1.
argument:: interp
0 hold, 1 linear, 2 cosine. Default 1.
argument:: mul
argument:: add

examples::
code::
{ Lifestoch.ar(110) * 0.3 ! 2 }.play;

{ Lifestoch.ar(110, 96, MouseX.kr(0.05, 1.5), 0.02) * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ Lifestoch.ar(90, 128, 0.6, MouseX.kr(0.005, 0.1)) * 0.25 ! 2 }.play;

{ Lifestoch.ar(120, 64, 0.3, 0.01, 1.0, MouseX.kr(0, 0.6)) * 0.25 ! 2 }.play;
::
